{
 "note": "Arena entity spawn tables from the level scripts. Records are 20 bytes: x, y, z as s16, a type word that is 4 for every entity, the entity type id, then an 8-byte tail.",
 "SCANNING_CAVEAT": "Records do NOT lie on one global 20-byte grid. An earlier pass assumed they did and silently dropped entities - it reported 1 lever on Mos when there are 3, because two of them sit at offsets 0x2DC and 0x2F0 which are off the grid anchored at 16. The scan now walks every 2-byte offset and only suppresses detections within 20 bytes of the previous one.",
