  "4": "unidentified"
 },
 "id_notes": {
  "220": "Three on Mos - two driving one bridge and one driving another, as reported from play.",
  "7 and 8": "IDENTIFIED. Both fall to the factory default 0x02015D90 (base class) and are live as asset 2522 (the hook, 3 on Mos and 12 on Jabba) and asset 2524 (the pad, 2 on Mos and 9 on Jabba). The earlier note calling them unidentified, and the retraction of their grapple reading, are both superseded.",
  "227": "The grapple. Three on Mos Eisley - one buildable and two static, matching play - and confirmed by the actor pointer chain to vtable 0x020FD6D8.",
  "75": "CAPTURE POINTS - CONFIRMED BY RUNTIME BEHAVIOUR, not just by count. In a Capture match on Jabbas Tower, player 1 (IG-88) carried the Carbonite to (16,54,0) and player 2 (Dengar) to (-16,54,0), the two ground-level id-75 records. Dengar was within 12 units of a capture point on 117 samples, IG-88 on 9. The four points are symmetric - (16,54,0), (-16,54,0), (0,81,27), (0,81,-26) - one per player, matching the reported behaviour that each is gated to its owner."
 },
