 },
 "RETRACTION_id_75": "id 75 was recorded as CAPTURE POINTS 'CONFIRMED BY RUNTIME BEHAVIOUR', because players carried the Carbonite to (16,54,0) and (-16,54,0) on Jabba. Those are genuinely type-0x4B objects, but a player moving to a place does not establish what is there. Every live 0x4B object carries asset 818 = BuildableGrapple. RAM at gpudump_walk_jabba/gpudump_walk_mos f12000: Jabba has FOUR - (16,54,0), (-16,54,0), (0,81,27), (0,81,-26) - and Mos has ONE at (-31,0,163). The 'four on Jabba, one per player' symmetry that made the capture-point reading plausible is a coincidence and does not survive Mos having a single one. 0x020170F4 `cmp r1,#0x4b` initialises it as a buildable (+0x194=0x20, +0x1AD=0, +0x1AC=7, +0x214=0). This is a known failure mode: matching instance counts against an expected inventory and calling it identification.",
 "RETRACTION_id_227": "id 227 (0xE3) was recorded as the grapple. It is the BRIDGE PLANK: the lever refuses to actuate a link whose type is not 0xE3 (0x0201FABC `cmp r0,#0xe3`), and the three live 0xE3 objects carry asset 4636 at the Mos bridge coordinates. vtable 0x020FD6D8 is shared by 34 spawn types, so it identifies nothing on its own - only +0x212 does."
